# Design: Capture and templates for mock scripts

## Problem
The mock agent could send fixed requests but could not read returned
identifiers, so it could never complete a stateful task: create a
clip, then act on the clip the backend minted. Scripts also could not
finish a turn, because disposition rule 7 (section 22.3) requires a
session event with kind turn.completed.

## Approach
- capture.body maps variable names to dot paths into the parsed JSON
  response; capture.headers maps names to response header names. A
  missing value fails the participant with MOCK_CAPTURE_FAILED.
- {{name}} substitution covers request path, header values, body
  objects (rendered deep), and the finalReport object.
- validateScriptTemplates runs at adapter prepare and at CLI script
  load, so an unknown variable never reaches the network.
- turn.completed fires only when the scripted flow reached a final
  message (finalText resolved or finalReport rendered) and no control
  or failure status cut it short. The empty default script stays
  agent_incomplete, which quickstart documents.

## Key Trade-offs
- Captured values never reach session events; only variable names are
  recorded, because a captured header can echo a credential.
- applyCredential rewrites the Authorization header last and drops
  script-supplied case variants, so a script cannot displace the
  minted token.

